        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#ffffff;font-family:Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:3px solid #0f172a;border-bottom:1px solid #0f172a;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>TWILITE ZONE · START HERE</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:500 clamp(40px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;text-wrap:balance;color:#0f172a'>What a graph is</h1><p style='margin:18px 0 0;max-width:36ch;font:italic 400 clamp(20px,3.6cqw,26px)/1.35 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#475569'>A node graph is a collection of nodes and edges. A node represents an idea, and an edge is a relationship between two ideas. You can describe anything in this way.</p></header></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>A node is an idea</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><span style='float:left;padding:6px 10px 0 0;font:500 68px/54px Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'>A</span> goal, a task, a question, a note, a link to somewhere else. Each node has its own text and its own status, so you can change one without touching the rest. &quot;Collect three quotes&quot; is a node.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>An edge is a relationship</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>An edge connects two nodes and says how they relate: this task belongs to that goal, this question blocks that task. The relationship is written down, so nobody has to work it out by rereading.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Together they make a graph</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Your kitchen project is a graph: one goal, its tasks, its open questions, and how they connect. Zoom out to see the whole project, or in to see a single task.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>A graph is kept as one file</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>A <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>.node</code> file is plain text with its own address. It says what is in the graph, what it is called, and how it should look. Because it is plain text, Twilite can open it, and so can ChatGPT or Gemini. That is why your AI can write one and you can read it.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Seen from outside, a graph is itself a node, so one graph can sit inside another.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Why not just a page?</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>A page is the right form for something you read straight through, and Twilite keeps those too. A project is not read from top to bottom. What needs you today depends on which tasks are open, which questions are unanswered, and which goals they serve.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>In a page, all of that lives in the prose, and you or your AI have to reread and re-sort it every time. A page expects one reading order. A graph has many paths: start from the overview, go into one branch, jump sideways to a related idea, and come back without losing the whole.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>In a graph the relationships are already written down. Change one status and everything connected to it can see. Your AI can add a task without rewriting your document. And a graph still has a page: when you are close enough to read it, you see its first face.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:40px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:stretch;gap:28px 32px'><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='primary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:12px;border-top:3px solid #6d28d9'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:500 26px/1.1 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a'>Start with your AI</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#475569'>Tell your AI what you want to keep track of, and it puts your project into a graph.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/library/starters/start-with-your-ai/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#6d28d9'>Start with your AI →</a></section></div><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='secondary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:500 22px/1.1 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a'>Go deeper</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#475569'>The same idea as a lesson, with an example to try and a check at the end.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/tutorial/core-concepts/what-is-a-node-graph/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#475569'>Read the lesson →</a></section></div><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='secondary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:500 22px/1.1 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a'>The primitives</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#475569'>The fifteen parts every graph is made of, each with a page of its own.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/library/primitives/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#475569'>Open the primitives →</a></section></div><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='secondary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:500 22px/1.1 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a'>The glossary</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#475569'>Every word the Twilite Zone uses, in the order a reader needs it.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/library/glossary/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#475569'>Read the glossary →</a></section></div></div></div></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "",
